  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1202 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nMild low temperatures will help take out some of the nip in our cold \nholiday weekend, but a new front arrives Sunday to bring a blustery \nday with winds suggested to come within a few mph of reaching wind \nadvisory criteria. The dry polar trough passing through the area is \nfairly progressive, and a flat zonal pattern over TX means only one \nday of cold air advection before the sfc winds take a turn back to \nsoutherlies. The daily warming trend continues as the next upstream \nupper low to impact the area is not expected until Thursday of next \nweek. This next system comes at a lower latitude and will be more \nsymmetrical in shape, so there could be a good opportunity for a \nreturn of rain chances. However the latest deterministic forecasts \nshow poor connectivity to the Pacific tropics, so the low (<50 \npercent) chances over mainly eastern counties might be the best we \ncan hope for.",
